# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1612.02058) is a technique for mitigating quantum noise in observable expectation value calculations. It lets you compute an unbiased estimate of the expectation values. This technique works by executing an ensemble of noisy circuits injected with the inverse of a learned noise model. The noise model is then approximated to a Pauli channel by using Pauli twirling (also known as [randomized compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325)). Such noise models can be learned efficiently and can be mitigated by using PEC (see [Probabilistic error cancellation with sparse Pauli-Lindblad models on noisy quantum\n"
"processors](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.09866) for more details).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1612.02058) ay isang teknik para bawasan ang quantum noise sa mga kalkulasyon ng observable expectation value. Pinapahintulutan ka nitong makakuha ng unbiased na tantiya ng mga expectation value. Gumagana ang teknik na ito sa pagpapatakbo ng isang ensemble ng mga noisy na circuit na may inject na inverse ng isang natutunang noise model. Ang noise model ay tinatantiya pagkatapos bilang isang Pauli channel gamit ang Pauli twirling (kilala rin bilang [randomized compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325)). Ang ganitong mga noise model ay mahusay na matututunan at maaaring ma-mitigate gamit ang PEC (tingnan ang [Probabilistic error cancellation with sparse Pauli-Lindblad models on noisy quantum\n"
"processors](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.09866) para sa higit pang detalye).\n"

