# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.09738) is a technique that mitigates measurement errors and is useful for estimating Pauli observable expectation values. It relies on measurement twirling (randomly injecting an `X` gate before the measurement and flipping the measured result), which diagonalizes the readout-error transfer matrix and makes it easy to invert. A rescaling term is learned from the diagonal noise channel by measuring twirled calibration circuits that were initialized in the zero state.\n"
msgstr "Ang [Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.09738) ay isang teknik na nagbabawas ng mga measurement error at kapaki-pakinabang sa pagtantiya ng mga Pauli observable expectation value. Umaasa ito sa measurement twirling (random na pag-i-inject ng `X` gate bago ang measurement at pag-flip sa nasukat na resulta), na dinadayagonal ang readout-error transfer matrix at ginagawang madaling i-invert. Natututunan ang isang rescaling term mula sa diagonal na noise channel sa pamamagitan ng pagsukat ng mga twirled na calibration circuit na na-initialize sa zero state.\n"

