# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute noisy, unmitigated expectation values {#compute-noisy-unmitigated-expectation-values}"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang mga noisy, unmitigated na expectation value {#compute-noisy-unmitigated-expectation-values}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs) contains a quantum circuit and a [samplex](/addons/samplomatic/guides/samplex-io) in a format suitable for the [Executor](/guides/get-started-with-executor) primitive. `MitigationTask.prepare` builds a `QuantumProgram` from the circuit, the observables and the parameter values, and boxes the circuit with the given boxing options. Set the ``measure_annotations`` boxing option to ``\"change_basis\"`` to rotate the measurements into the required bases, and add ``add_tags: \"unique_box\"`` so the simulator can map a noise model onto the circuit's boxes. The program is Pauli twirled by default, which on hardware turns coherent noise into the Pauli noise that the mitigation methods assume. `num_randomizations` sets how many twirled instances of each circuit are sampled and `shots_per_randomization` sets how many shots each instance receives, so their product is the shot limit per circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs) ay naglalaman ng isang quantum circuit at isang [samplex](/addons/samplomatic/guides/samplex-io) sa format na angkop para sa [Executor](/guides/get-started-with-executor) primitive. Binubuo ng `MitigationTask.prepare` ang isang `QuantumProgram` mula sa circuit, mga observable at mga parameter value, at ibinabox ang circuit gamit ang ibinigay na mga boxing option. Itakda ang boxing option na ``measure_annotations`` sa ``\"change_basis\"`` para i-rotate ang mga measurement sa kinakailangang mga basis, at idagdag ang ``add_tags: \"unique_box\"`` para maimapa ng simulator ang isang noise model sa mga box ng circuit. Pauli twirled ang programa bilang default, na sa hardware ay ginagawang Pauli noise ang coherent noise na ipinapalagay ng mga paraan ng mitigation. Itinatakda ng `num_randomizations` kung ilang twirled na instance ng bawat circuit ang sina-sample at itinatakda ng `shots_per_randomization` kung ilang shot ang natatanggap ng bawat instance, kaya ang kanilang produkto ang shot limit bawat circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you have QPU access, you can execute the program with an `Executor` built from a backend of the `QiskitRuntimeService`.  This examples uses an `AerSimulator` to run the program locally. Its `layer_noise_model` simulator option injects a random Pauli-Lindblad noise model on every layer of entangling gates, generated with `random_pauli_lindblad_noise` from `qiskit-mitigation` with an error per layered gate (EPLG) of ``0.003``, typical of current Heron QPUs.\n"
msgstr "Kung may access ka sa QPU, maaari mong patakbuhin ang programa gamit ang `Executor` na binuo mula sa isang backend ng `QiskitRuntimeService`. Gumagamit ang halimbawang ito ng `AerSimulator` para patakbuhin ang programa nang lokal. Ang simulator option nitong `layer_noise_model` ay nag-i-inject ng random na Pauli-Lindblad noise model sa bawat layer ng entangling gates, na nabuo gamit ang `random_pauli_lindblad_noise` mula sa `qiskit-mitigation` na may error per layered gate (EPLG) na ``0.003``, na tipikal sa mga kasalukuyang Heron QPU.\n"

