# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the entangling layers' noise {#learn-the-entangling-layers-noise}"
msgstr "Alamin ang noise ng mga entangling layer {#learn-the-entangling-layers-noise}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC starts by learning the twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit. If you assume a Markovian noise model, the depth of the circuit is assumed to not affect the noise channel of a given entangling layer.  Therefore, only the noise model of each unique layer of entangling gates should be learned. The circuit used in this guide can be split into two unique layers. Designing circuits to have a minimal set of unique entangling layers is important if you want to learn a noise model, since the unique layers must be learned independently. If you have too many unique layers in your circuit, noise learning can become infeasible due to the sampling cost of learning many layers.\n"
msgstr "Nagsisimula ang PEC sa pag-aaral ng twirled noise model ng bawat layer ng entangling gates sa circuit. Kung ipinapalagay mo ang Markovian na noise model, ipinapalagay na hindi naaapektuhan ng depth ng circuit ang noise channel ng isang entangling layer. Kaya, ang noise model lang ng bawat natatanging layer ng entangling gates ang kailangang matutunan. Ang circuit na ginamit sa gabay na ito ay maaaring hatiin sa dalawang natatanging layer. Mahalagang idisenyo ang mga circuit na may pinakamaliit na set ng natatanging entangling layer kung gusto mong matutunan ang isang noise model, dahil kailangang matutunan nang hiwalay ang mga natatanging layer. Kung masyadong marami ang natatanging layer sa circuit mo, maaaring maging imposible ang noise learning dahil sa sampling cost ng pag-aaral ng maraming layer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`qiskit-noise-learning` is used to learn the noise. The learner repeats each layer _`fragment_depths`_ times in its learning circuits, twirls each circuit _`num_randomizations`_ times, and fits the decay of the measured fidelities to a Pauli-Lindblad model. These parameters can effect the accuracy of the learned model. The more accurate the learned noise model is, the more accurate the noise cancellation will be.\n"
"The following code draws the learned noise model with the two layers merged into one map. Each qubit is a pie of its weight-1 X, Y and Z rates summed over the two layers, and each edge shows the learned weight-2 rates. For example, a rate of ``3e-4`` means that error occurs on roughly three of every 10,000 uses of the layer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagamit ang `qiskit-noise-learning` para matutunan ang noise. Inuulit ng learner ang bawat layer nang _`fragment_depths`_ beses sa mga learning circuit nito, nagta-twirl ng bawat circuit nang _`num_randomizations`_ beses, at ifi-fit ang pagbaba ng mga nasukat na fidelity sa isang Pauli-Lindblad model. Maaaring makaapekto ang mga parameter na ito sa katumpakan ng natutunang model. Kung mas tumpak ang natutunang noise model, mas tumpak din ang pagkansela ng noise.\n"
"Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na code ang natutunang noise model kung saan pinagsama sa isang mapa ang dalawang layer. Ang bawat qubit ay isang pie ng weight-1 na X, Y at Z rate nito na pinagsama sa dalawang layer, at ipinapakita ng bawat edge ang mga natutunang weight-2 rate. Halimbawa, ang rate na ``3e-4`` ay nangangahulugang nagaganap ang error na iyon sa humigit-kumulang tatlo sa bawat 10,000 gamit ng layer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Readout noise mitigation is done in post-processing by using TREX, as opposed to the **gate** noise model, which is required for the program preparation in order to inject the anti-noise that corresponds to the learned noise model.\n"
"Therefore, the readout noise can be either executed and learned when learning the gates' noise, or when executing the mitigated program. Learning the readout noise alongside the gate noise might be beneficial for learning a self-consistent noise model (see [Disambiguating Pauli noise in quantum computers](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.22629) for example). In cases where the gate noise and the readout noise are separated in the noise model, it is recommended that you learn the readout noise when executing the mitigated program to avoid drift in the noise between the when it was learned and executed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagawa ang readout noise mitigation sa post-processing gamit ang TREX, kabaligtaran ng **gate** noise model, na kailangan sa paghahanda ng programa para ma-inject ang anti-noise na tumutugma sa natutunang noise model.\n"
"Kaya, ang readout noise ay maaaring patakbuhin at matutunan habang inaalam ang noise ng mga gate, o habang pinapatakbo ang mitigated na programa. Maaaring makatulong ang pag-aaral ng readout noise kasabay ng gate noise para matutunan ang self-consistent na noise model (tingnan ang [Disambiguating Pauli noise in quantum computers](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.22629) bilang halimbawa). Sa mga kasong magkahiwalay ang gate noise at readout noise sa noise model, inirerekomendang alamin ang readout noise habang pinapatakbo ang mitigated na programa para maiwasan ang drift ng noise sa pagitan ng pagkakatuto nito at ng pagpapatakbo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide, the readout noise is learned while executing the mitigated program by using TREX calibration circuit.\n"
msgstr "Sa gabay na ito, natututunan ang readout noise habang pinapatakbo ang mitigated na programa gamit ang TREX calibration circuit.\n"

