# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare a combined PEC and TREX program {#prepare-a-combined-pec-and-trex-program}"
msgstr "Maghanda ng pinagsamang PEC at TREX program {#prepare-a-combined-pec-and-trex-program}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we prepare both a `TREX` and a `PEC` task, and add the `TREX` task as a variable to the `PEC` task. This ensures that all the required properties needed for TREX mitigation are added to the PEC mitigated item (like measurement twirling). The injected noise is sampled once per randomization, so the statistical error of PEC is controlled by the number of randomizations rather than the shots per randomization. Thus, many randomizations are used - each with few shots - keeping the total number of shots the same as for the unmitigated program.\n"
msgstr "Dito, naghahanda tayo ng parehong `TREX` at `PEC` task, at idinaragdag ang `TREX` task bilang variable sa `PEC` task. Tinitiyak nito na naidaragdag sa PEC mitigated na item ang lahat ng kinakailangang property para sa TREX mitigation (tulad ng measurement twirling). Isang beses sa bawat randomization sina-sample ang ini-inject na noise, kaya ang statistical error ng PEC ay kinokontrol ng bilang ng mga randomization sa halip na ng mga shot bawat randomization. Kaya, maraming randomization ang ginagamit - bawat isa ay may kaunting shot - habang pinananatiling pareho ang kabuuang bilang ng shot sa unmitigated na programa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The TREX calibration circuit is added to the program in order to learn the readout noise while executing the program. The TREX calibration circuit is very shallow, which makes additional randomizations for it to be relatively cheap and allows the readout noise to be learned more accurately.\n"
msgstr "Idinaragdag ang TREX calibration circuit sa programa para matutunan ang readout noise habang pinapatakbo ang programa. Napakababaw ng TREX calibration circuit, kaya medyo mura ang karagdagang mga randomization nito at nagpapahintulot na mas tumpak na matutunan ang readout noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examine shot overhead, execute the program, and post-process {#examine-shot-overhead-execute-the-program-and-post-process}"
msgstr "Suriin ang shot overhead, patakbuhin ang programa, at mag-post-process {#examine-shot-overhead-execute-the-program-and-post-process}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC returns an unbiased expectation value estimation, with a cost of large shot overhead. The required shot overhead can be approximated by calculating the circuit gamma factor, which reflects the effect of the learned noise model on the circuit. By default, the number of randomization of the PEC task is scaled by the approximate amount of shot overhead required to have an unbiased estimation (~$\\gamma^2$). To avoid this automatic scale, you can set the parameter `scale_randomizations_by_gamma` to `False`. The shots overhead is capped by the `max_sampling_overhead` parameter.\n"
msgstr "Nagbabalik ang PEC ng unbiased na pagtantiya ng expectation value, kapalit ng malaking shot overhead. Matatantiya ang kinakailangang shot overhead sa pagkalkula ng circuit gamma factor, na sumasalamin sa epekto ng natutunang noise model sa circuit. Bilang default, ini-scale ang bilang ng randomization ng PEC task ayon sa tinatayang dami ng shot overhead na kailangan para sa unbiased na pagtantiya (~$\\gamma^2$). Para maiwasan ang awtomatikong scale na ito, maaari mong itakda ang parameter na `scale_randomizations_by_gamma` sa `False`. Nililimitahan ng parameter na `max_sampling_overhead` ang shots overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You should review the number of shots required by PEC to reach unbiased estimation before execution to decide whether this amount is affordable, as this scales exponentially in the noise rates and circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "Dapat mong suriin ang bilang ng shot na kailangan ng PEC para makamit ang unbiased na pagtantiya bago ang pagpapatakbo para magpasya kung abot-kaya ang halagang ito, dahil exponential itong tumataas ayon sa mga noise rate at circuit depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the mitigated expectation values {#compare-the-mitigated-expectation-values}"
msgstr "Ihambing ang mga mitigated na expectation value {#compare-the-mitigated-expectation-values}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, plot the expectation value of each observable. PEC + TREX recovers the exact expectation values within its error bars, while the unmitigated result is biased well below it.\n"
msgstr "Panghuli, i-plot ang expectation value ng bawat observable. Nababawi ng PEC + TREX ang eksaktong mga expectation value sa loob ng mga error bar nito, habang ang unmitigated na resulta ay may bias na mas mababa nang malayo rito.\n"

